                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Start with ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\frac{36}{48}",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ". Find two different ways to get to simplest form, using at least two divisions by common factors in each route.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\div4$, then $\\div3$; or $\\div2$, then $\\div6$. Both give $\\frac34$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{36}{48}&=\\frac{36\\div4}{48\\div4}=\\frac9{12}\\\\\\frac9{12}&=\\frac{9\\div3}{12\\div3}=\\frac34\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{36}{48}&=\\frac{36\\div2}{48\\div2}=\\frac{18}{24}\\\\\\frac{18}{24}&=\\frac{18\\div6}{24\\div6}=\\frac34\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q8-n",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "n",
        "prompt": "Multiply the divisors used in each route in part m.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4\\times3=12$; $2\\times6=12$.",
          "worked": "$4\\times3=12$; $2\\times6=12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q8-o",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "o",
        "prompt": "How do these products compare with the HCF of 36 and 48?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Both equal the HCF, 12.",
          "worked": "Both equal the HCF, 12.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q8-p",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "p",
        "prompt": "Explain why the products equal the HCF.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Successive divisions equal division by their product. Simplest form removes the full common factor.",
          "worked": "Dividing the numerator and denominator successively is equivalent to dividing each by the product of the divisors. Reaching simplest form removes the full common factor, so that product is the HCF.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
